{"title":"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find  the  radius  of  the  inscribed  circle  of  a  triangle  with  sides  of  length  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />,  and  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/78916550838bd31d66e4cdefbc366edb11fd00bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$37$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/0/020e512dd815228f54a776d1ec98ba1c8899250d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) }\\frac{9}{2}\\qquad \\text{(B) }\\frac{7}{2}\\qquad \\text{(C) }4\\qquad \\text{(D) }-\\sqrt{2}\\qquad \\text{(E) }4\\sqrt{5}\\qquad \\text{(F) }6\\qquad \\\\ \\text{(G) }\\frac{11}{2}\\qquad \\text{(H) }\\frac{13}{2}\\qquad \\text{(I) }\\text{none of the above}\\qquad \\text{(J) }1\\qquad \\text{(K) }\\text{no triangle exists}\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"584\" height=\"75\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since we know three sides, we can calculate the semiperimeter and area and use the results to find the radius of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Incircle\" title=\"Incircle\">incircle</a>.  The semiperimeter of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/2/d72fab114091dd6c12714af58eb2392247f76bf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac12 \\cdot (13 + 30 + 37) = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"178\" height=\"21\" />.  By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Heron%27s_Formula\" title=\"Heron&#39;s Formula\">Heron's Formula</a>, the area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/7/387a39a474d9f0dfb64b1de3f498a831c80ca890.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{40 \\cdot 27 \\cdot 10 \\cdot 3} = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"169\" height=\"18\" />.  Since the radius of the incircle times the semiperimeter equals the area, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/349026629cf2291cdf8e3cd7ef1f329b6fe87cb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = sr$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" /> the radius of the incircle must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a56abb4e2caae24894da5eb46f039f26a2a7f850.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{180}{40} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\tfrac{9}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest\" title=\"2006 iTest\">2006 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 iTest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 